{"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04ST", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0003": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0004": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0005": "$1$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\in \\Ob((\\Sch/S)_{fppf})$", "MATH_0007": "$y \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{Y}_U)$", "MATH_0008": "$2$", "MATH_0009": "$(\\Sch/U)_{fppf} \\times_{y, \\mathcal{Y}} \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0010": "$(\\Sch/U)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0011": "$f_y : V_y \\to U$", "MATH_0012": "$$\n(\\Sch/V_y)_{fppf}\n\\longrightarrow\n(\\Sch/U)_{fppf} \\times_{y, \\mathcal{Y}} \\mathcal{X}.\n$$", "MATH_0013": "$f_y$", "MATH_0014": "$(\\Sch/V_y)_{fppf} \\to\n(\\Sch/U)_{fppf} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{Y}\n\\to (\\Sch/U)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0015": "\\begin{equation}\n\\label{equation-representable}\n\\vcenter{\n\\xymatrix{\nV_y \\ar@{~>}[r] \\ar[d]_{f_y} &\n(\\Sch/V_y)_{fppf} \\ar[d] \\ar[r] &\n\\mathcal{X} \\ar[d]^f \\\\\nU \\ar@{~>}[r] &\n(\\Sch/U)_{fppf} \\ar[r]^-y &\n\\mathcal{Y}\n}\n}\n\\end{equation}", "MATH_0016": "$2$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-definition-representable-map-categories-fibred-in-groupoids}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{section-representable}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{equation-morphisms-schemes}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2f941f5aecbaf450491a89d709e44a73f1c6702b4128d308b8204f15c58be87b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3a1a6bcbc984e0dcf3ca610bc20cb48dbb087bd947a99b173eb175f22ec554eb", "source_text": "\n\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001>, <MATH_0002> be categories fibred in groupoids\nover <MATH_0003>. Let <MATH_0004>\nbe a <TEXTITOPEN_0001>representable <MATH_0005>-morphism<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>, see\nCategories, Definition\n<REF_0001>.\nThis means that for every <MATH_0006> and\nany <MATH_0007> the <MATH_0008>-fibre product\n<MATH_0009>\nis representable as a category fibred in groupoids over\n<MATH_0010>. Choose a representing object <MATH_0011>\nand an equivalence\n<MATH_0012>\nThe morphism <MATH_0013> corresponds to the projection\n<MATH_0014>\nSee Section <REF_0002>,\nEquation (<REF_0003>). We represent this by the diagram\n<MATH_0015>\nwhere the squiggly arrows represent the <MATH_0016>-Yoneda embedding.\nHere are some lemmas about this notion that work in great generality\n(namely, they work for categories fibred in groupoids over any\nbase category which has fibre products).\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:18cc6857f70ea27975fb268f2b05cc87182cd66997b9ec99b16312a2d3edb74d", "unit_id": "tag:04ST:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04ST", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0003": "$1$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$$\n(\\Sch/X)_{fppf} \\longrightarrow (\\Sch/Y)_{fppf}\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$1$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-morphism-schemes-gives-representable-transformation}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:bbc49933f0f69c5781415ef12c47697a07c66dfdf1e935bc66f20df6bdd492d9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fd36ca40bea74cab8586be7fb58bceaaa729902287f8570f1febc722501bfd7b", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of <MATH_0002>.\nThen the <MATH_0003>-morphism induced by <MATH_0004>\n<MATH_0005>\nis a representable <MATH_0006>-morphism.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ff7237fb3d15579e7c967efbae0d7062f61c5ea8a15cb18e5d1e8c86c4bde396", "unit_id": "tag:02ZR:statement"}
{"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04ST", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b7e875813bc823b930144ad92ef10071c63bf5ee72ee22d185fe012f8ad2b625", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9544b7ebae55aa686d546c5aaddafca96a0b6c50467b801492816a95817bf8db", "source_text": "This is formal and relies only on the fact that\nthe category <MATH_0001> has fibre products.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5f0432aec7c98ba70c2ea88e8fa78fc855f561086c7b872a35dbf23691e85f3f", "unit_id": "tag:02ZR:proof"}
{"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04ST", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sch_{fppf}$", "MATH_0003": "$2$", "MATH_0004": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{X}' \\ar[r] \\ar[d]_{f'} & \\mathcal{X} \\ar[d]^f \\\\\n\\mathcal{Y}' \\ar[r] & \\mathcal{Y}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$1$", "MATH_0006": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0007": "$f$", "MATH_0008": "$f'$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-representable-morphism-equivalent}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:de61c5920a5b14bb01fb1e9cf53a22c2819148fcbbd7dba7ff553e91aca76504", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:032e1dfbd9379102cd1edcbb81c8216e761a8d8fed4137b9e7338d181825d408", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an object of <MATH_0002>.\nConsider a <MATH_0003>-commutative diagram\n<MATH_0004>\nof <MATH_0005>-morphisms of categories fibred in groupoids over\n<MATH_0006>.\nAssume the horizontal arrows are equivalences.\nThen <MATH_0007> is representable if and only if <MATH_0008> is representable.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6da05dad9e091045dc3e2d5caaf9b442fffbcf9fd2eb683fd56ea7aa9c609120", "unit_id": "tag:0456:statement"}
